1
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:05,840
(Raj:)Okay, in Avatar
when they have sex on Pandora...

2
00:00:06,006 --> 00:00:07,546
(Raj:)...they hook up their ponytails.

3
00:00:07,716 --> 00:00:11,176
(Raj:)So we know their ponytails
are like their junk.

4
00:00:11,344 --> 00:00:12,844
(Howard:)Yeah. So?

5
00:00:13,013 --> 00:00:14,973
(Raj:)When they ride horses
and fly on birds...

6
00:00:15,140 --> 00:00:17,640
(Raj:)-...they also use their ponytails.
-Your point?

7
00:00:17,809 --> 00:00:22,019
(Raj:)My point is if I were a horse or a bird I'd
be very nervous around James Cameron.

8
00:00:23,523 --> 00:00:27,483
(Sheldon:)It amazes me how you constantly
obsess over fictional details...

9
00:00:27,652 --> 00:00:30,652
...when there are important things
in the world to worry about.

10
00:00:30,822 --> 00:00:34,322
(Sheldon:)For example, why wasn't William
Shatner in the new Star Trek movie?

11
00:00:34,951 --> 00:00:37,541
(Leonard:)Hey, Sheldon,
I was up in the administration office...

12
00:00:37,704 --> 00:00:40,334
(Leonard:)...and I happened to overhear
the name of the winner...

13
00:00:40,498 --> 00:00:42,458
(Leonard:)...of the
Chancellor's Award for Science.

14
00:00:42,625 --> 00:00:46,375
You wanna rub my nose in the fact my
contributions are being overlooked again?

15
00:00:46,546 --> 00:00:48,926
(Sheldon:)I am the William Shatner
of theoretical physics.

16
00:00:50,008 --> 00:00:51,048
(Sheldon:)All right, I'll play.

17
00:00:51,217 --> 00:00:54,717
(Sheldon:)What self-important preening fraud
are they honoring this year?

18
00:00:54,888 --> 00:00:57,058
(Leonard:)Oh, I'm so glad you asked it like that.
You.

19
00:00:59,726 --> 00:01:01,226
(Sheldon:)-I won?
-You won.

20
00:01:02,228 --> 00:01:03,938
(Sheldon:)I won.

21
00:01:04,105 --> 00:01:05,355
(Sheldon:)This is astonishing.

22
00:01:05,523 --> 00:01:08,063
(Sheldon:)Not that I won the award.
No one deserves it more.

23
00:01:08,234 --> 00:01:10,694
(Sheldon:)Actually, I guess I misspoke.
It's not astonishing.

24
00:01:10,862 --> 00:01:12,652
It's more like inevitable.

25
00:01:13,239 --> 00:01:15,279
(Sheldon:)Not sure what to do.
Maybe call my mother.

26
00:01:15,450 --> 00:01:17,990
Wait. I'm gonna conduct
an interview with myself...

27
00:01:18,161 --> 00:01:19,201
(Sheldon:)...and post it online.

28
00:01:23,374 --> 00:01:24,704
(Raj:)Well, good for him.

29
00:01:24,876 --> 00:01:26,876
(Howard:)Yeah, the one thing
the William Shatner...

30
00:01:27,045 --> 00:01:31,025
(Howard:)...of theoretical physics needed
was an ego boost.

